From 08aa4e2b2dd6ff396d03bf546d17084d865a5f05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:52:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Withdraw prepared approvals when Desktop pauses for
 update

Terminal batches wait for consent before registering in-flight execution, so the mid-tool watcher skipped their 300-second approval waits. Withdraw unanswered requests using existing first-settlement semantics, only for resumable paused turns. Never grant consent; retain re-ask notice and ordinary boundary persistence.

Proof: new wait regression RED before fix; 185 tests across 13 pause/batch files GREEN. Hook/Stop guard mutant fails both controls; resumability mutant fails opt-out control. Real AIAgent two-terminal preparation test persists both results, executes neither command and pauses without another model call.
---
